I'm excited to share some of our work at @thinkymachines. As models get more intelligent, the bottleneck is increasingly how quickly and seamlessly we can access their intelligence. Today, we are sharing a preview of how we think about human-AI collaboration.

@thinkymachines: "People talk, listen, watch, think, and collaborate at the same time, in real time. We've designed an AI that works with people the same way. We share our approach, early results, and a quick look at our model in action."

Interaction models move beyond turn-based AI interfaces by handling multimodal, real-time collaboration natively across audio, video, and text.

My first share since joining @thinkymachines. It's fun working with this team on real-time multimodal interaction. Vision in turn-based models felt like flipping through photos, while continuous video presents a different challenge. Visual proactivity is essential, and I'm grateful to have worked on this alongside @liliyu_lili, @rown, and the rest of the team.

